.TH FBDESKTOP 1 "2026-09-10" "flux-tools 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fbdesktop \- create desktop entries for FluxBox environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbdesktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbdesktop
creates the default Flux application entries in the appropriate applications directory on first run. It handles both system-wide and user-specific desktop file creation based on user privileges. Once initialized, it does not recreate entries removed by the user.
The MIME application cache is refreshed on every run, including after initialization, so applications can resolve the file handlers declared by the existing desktop entries. User-selected default applications are not changed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications
System-wide application directory (root user)
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications
User-specific application directory
.TP
.I ~/.fluxbox/fbdesktop.initialized
Marker indicating that the default application entries have already been created
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update-desktop-database (1)
.SH AUTHOR
crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>
.SH NOTES
User entries honor XDG_DATA_HOME. Initialization errors do not create the success marker, and existing entries are preserved during retries. Hidden image viewers use NoDisplay and retain concrete MIME handlers. System entries and MIME caches remain readable with a private caller umask.
